TUnit uses `[Before(...)]` and `[After(...)]` attributes with a scope enum, plus class hooks via `IAsyncInitializer` / `IAsyncDisposable` on fixtures. Here's a sketch for each scope:

## 1. Before every test in a class

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public void ResetDatabase()
    {
        // Runs before each [Test] in this class
        InMemoryDb.Reset();
    }
}
```

## 2. Once before/after all tests in a class (class-scoped fixture)

```csharp
public class SharedFixture : IAsyncInitializer, IAsyncDisposable
{
    public SqliteConnection Connection { get; private set; }

    public Task InitializeAsync()
    {
        Connection = new SqliteConnection("Data Source=:memory:");
        return Connection.OpenAsync();
    }

    public async ValueTask DisposeAsync()
    {
        await Connection.DisposeAsync();
    }
}

[ClassDataSource<SharedFixture>(Shared = SharedType.PerClass)]
public class MyTests(SharedFixture fixture)
{
    [Test]
    public async Task QueryWorks()
    {
        // Use fixture.Connection
    }
}
```

Or with hook methods directly:

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static void OpenConnection() { /* once before first test */ }

    [After(Class)]
    public static void CloseConnection() { /* once after last test */ }
}
```

## 3. Once before/after all tests in the assembly

```csharp
public class GlobalSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static void StartWireMock()
    {
        WireMockServer.Start();
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static void StopWireMock()
    {
        WireMockServer.Stop();
    }
}
```

The class can live anywhere in the assembly — TUnit discovers it automatically. Methods must be `static`.

## 4. Once at the very start/end of the entire test session

```csharp
public class SessionSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations()
    {
        await Database.MigrateAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDown()
    {
        await Database.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

`TestSession` is the outermost scope — it wraps all assemblies if multiple are loaded.

---

**Summary table:**

| Scope | Attribute | Must be static? |
|-------|-----------|-----------------|
| Per-test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | No |
| Per-class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | Yes |
| Per-assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | Yes |
| Per-session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | Yes |

All hook methods can be `async Task` or synchronous `void`. The enum values come from `TUnit.Core.HookType`.
